   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate377.YaqP5I/probe.ts\" head\nbun \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate377.YaqP5I/probe.ts\" base",
    "output": "Relevant C1 rows:\n{\"revision\":\"head\",\"mode\":\"C1\",\"exitCode\":0,\"backgroundAlive\":false,\"continuedWriting\":false}\n{\"revision\":\"base\",\"mode\":\"C1\",\"exitCode\":0,\"backgroundAlive\":true,\"continuedWriting\":true}"
   },
   "evidence": "The probe independently launched an unmarked, detached native shell after invocation start, using the invocation's temporary cwd, and waited for its launcher to exit. HEAD selects it through `if (parents.get(pid) !== 1) return false`, the birth-time check, and `return directories.some(...)`; no marker or ancestry connects it to the invocation. Lines 197\u2013199 add qualifying hidden orphans to the marked set, and proc.ts:202\u2013207 signals them. Base only signals the invocation's process group and leaves this independent job alive. This differs from G1's shared scratch-root mechanism and G2's recycled identifiers."
